From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Floyd <git@notmy.space>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 08:27:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: simple: Park the focus lens when the camera stops

CameraSensor opens the lens subdevice when the camera is created and
keeps it open for the camera manager's lifetime, so with a long-lived
client such as WirePlumber a VCM driver like dw9719 never
runtime-suspends. Whatever position autofocus last set is held with the
coil energised until the next capture: on the Moto G Play (2024) the
lens stayed at code 552 of 1023 after a capture, about half the
actuator's full-scale current, indefinitely.

Move the lens to its minimum position in stopDevice(), after the
software ISP (and with it the IPA) has stopped and can no longer move
it.

Signed-off-by: William Floyd <git@notmy.space>
---
 src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
index 553e4c6..91bbcbf 100644
--- a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
@@ -1768,6 +1768,20 @@ void SimplePipelineHandler::stopDevice(Camera *camera)
 			data->swIsp_->stop();
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Park the focus lens. The lens subdevice stays open for as long as
+	 * the camera manager lives, so a VCM driver never runtime-suspends
+	 * and a lens left mid-travel keeps drawing coil current until the
+	 * next capture. The IPA is stopped by now and cannot move it again.
+	 */
+	CameraLens *focusLens = data->sensor_->focusLens();
+	if (focusLens) {
+		const ControlInfoMap &lensInfo = focusLens->controls();
+		auto it = lensInfo.find(V4L2_CID_FOCUS_ABSOLUTE);
+		if (it != lensInfo.end())
+			focusLens->setFocusPosition(it->second.min().get<int32_t>());
+	}
+
 	video->streamOff();
 	video->releaseBuffers();
 
